---
// The community guidelines of the circle in the Songdance app. Every member
// accepts them at first sign-in (with the terms and the privacy policy), and
// each space in the app shows the short version — the six lines in
// songdance-app, apps/api/import/mighty/config.ts (GUIDELINES). This page is
// the full text the App Store (guideline 1.2) and Google Play (User Generated
// Content policy) ask for: what is not allowed, how to report and block, and
// what we do. Article 21 of the terms points here.
import SiteLayout from '../components/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Community guidelines — Songdance"
  description="What keeps the Songdance circle safe: what we ask of every member, what is not allowed, and how to report something."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="The circle"
    title="Community guidelines"
    lede="The circle is held, not moderated into silence. A few things keep it safe for everyone."
  />

  <section class="sd-section sd-prose sd-legal">
    <div class="sd-prose-inner">
      <p class="sd-legal-updated">Last update: 8 October 2026</p>

      <p class="sd-legal-intro">The circle is the community inside the Songdance app: the spaces where members of our courses share what they find in their practice, ask questions and answer each other. It is open to adults only. Everyone accepts these guidelines, together with our <a href="/terms">terms</a> and <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>, before they can read or post.</p>

      <h2>What we ask of every member</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>What is shared here stays here.</strong> Someone else’s story is not yours to carry out of this space. Don’t copy, screenshot, record or pass on what another member shares.</li>
        <li><strong>Meet what someone brings with acknowledgment.</strong> No fixing, no advice they did not ask for, no diagnosis.</li>
        <li><strong>A facilitator holds space; the person sounding does their own work.</strong> Nobody here speaks for anyone else’s body.</li>
        <li><strong>Nothing is sold in this circle.</strong> Share your work by being in it, not by advertising.</li>
        <li><strong>If a post or a comment lands wrongly, report it.</strong> A host reads every report.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What is not allowed</h2>
      <p>We have <strong>no tolerance for objectionable content or abusive behaviour</strong>. That includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>harassment, bullying, threats or intimidation, in posts, comments or practice invitations</li>
        <li>hate or discrimination against anyone for who they are, including their origin, religion, gender, sexual orientation, disability or age</li>
        <li>sexual content or nudity, and anything that sexualises a minor</li>
        <li>violent or graphic content, and anything that encourages self-harm</li>
        <li>medical, psychological or therapeutic advice or diagnosis given to another member</li>
        <li>advertising, selling, or recruiting members as clients, followers or customers</li>
        <li>sharing another person’s personal details, messages, pictures or recordings without their permission</li>
        <li>pretending to be someone else, or a Songdance host</li>
        <li>spam, scams, and anything illegal</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to report, and how to block</h2>
      <p>Every post, comment and profile in the app has <strong>Report</strong>. A report goes straight to the hosts and to us, and we look at every report within 24 hours. The person you report is not told who reported them.</p>
      <p>You can also <strong>Block</strong> any member. After that, neither of you sees the other’s posts, comments or profile, and they cannot invite you to practice.</p>
      <p>You can always write to us at <a href="mailto:support@songdance.co">support@songdance.co</a>, about anything in the circle.</p>

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <p>Depending on what happened, we remove the post or comment, have a word with the member, pause their posting or practice invitations, or suspend or close their account. Where content is illegal or someone is in danger, we may pass it on to the authorities. What we decide is up to us, guided by these guidelines and <a href="/terms">article 21 of our terms</a>.</p>

      <h2>When something is too much to carry</h2>
      <p>The circle is a place to be witnessed, not an emergency service, and it is not therapy. If you or someone else is in danger, call your local emergency number. If you are struggling, please reach out to a doctor, a therapist or a crisis line where you live.</p>

      <div class="sd-legal-block">
        <p><strong>SONGDANCE BV</strong></p>
        <p>Beaupréstraat 13, 8310 Brugge, Belgium</p>
        <p>Email: <a href="mailto:support@songdance.co">support@songdance.co</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
